{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 5 — blast radius of the lean projection, MEASURED (do not re-derive)\n\nPlan-review round 6 blocked (`G1G2`) arguing that widening `LEAN_OMITTED_FIELDS` inside\n`list_states` would silently strip `authorship_ledger`/`attestations`/`signature`/`keyring`\nfrom three non-MCP consumers. **That scenario does NOT materialise.** Measured against this\nstore rather than reasoned about:\n\n| caller | exact call | rows | the four signature fields |\n|---|---|---:|---|\n| `validate.py:67` (`_raw_tickets`) | `list_states(tracker)` — `query=None` | 2,863 | **PRESENT** |\n| `next_batch.py:144` | `list_states(tracker, TicketQuery(status=\"open,in_progress\"))` | 62 | **PRESENT** |\n| `reads_cli.py:344` (CLI `list` arm) | `list_states(tracker, TicketQuery(include_body=False))` | 2,863 | **DROPPED** |\n\nMechanism: `TicketQuery.include_body` defaults to **`True`** (`ticket_query.py:52`), and\n`list_states(tracker)` with `query=None` constructs a default `TicketQuery()`\n(`reads.py:437`). Only a caller that explicitly passes `include_body=False` narrows.\n\n**So the blast radius is exactly three surfaces, all already documented as breaking:** MCP\n`list_tickets`, MCP `ready_tickets`, and CLI `rebar list`. `validate` and `next_batch` are\nunaffected and need no `full=True` compensation.\n\n### Round-6 advisories that are artifacts, not defects\n\nTwo `E4` advisories report that `LEAN_OMITTED_FIELDS` and `_mcp_reads._discovery_rows` \"do not\nexist anywhere in the repo\". True at `origin/main`, which is what the reviewer reads; false\nafter the change. An AC that cites symbols the change CREATES cannot be verified by a reviewer\nreading the pre-change tree — worth phrasing future ACs as \"introduces X\" rather than naming X\nas if it exists.\n\n### Plan-review history on this ticket (6 rounds, none forced)\n\n| round | blocking | nature |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 1 | `T1` — description contradicted sibling `unreal-milky-sloth` |\n| 2 | 3 | ACs under-specified the implementation (`G1G2`/`G6`/`T8`) |\n| 3 | 2 | **real bug**: `ready_tickets` refusal named filters it does not accept |\n| 4 | 1 | `P4` — description 9,226 chars over the 8,000 cap |\n| 5 | 1 | `G1G2` — MCP-tool vs library layer conflated in AC wording |\n| 6 | 1 | `G1G2` — AC-2 edit locus + unenumerated consumers (this comment) |\n\n`P4` structural signals never flagged oversize (`ac_items` 9 vs cap 25; `file_impact` 9 vs cap\n30). The pressure is not item count — it is that AC-2 must carry a four-layer argument (one\nshared function -> two backends -> library untouched -> applied at the MCP tool layer -> three\nsurfaces narrow -> three consumers do not) inside an 8,000-char cap. Rounds 5 and 6 both blocked\non that single AC, and at 7,678 chars there were 322 left, less than the enumeration round 6\nasked for. That is why this work is being split A (projection) / B (bound), B depending on A."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787958658305788001,"uuid":"4560a1c0-9713-4ef5-b3c5-86dcbeb314b1"}